  "major": "journalism-sociology-ba-b16220de",
  "major_name": "Journalism and Sociology",
  "degree": "BA",
  "campus": "Boston",
  "college": "College of Arts, Media and Design",
  "overview_text": "This combined major offers students an opportunity to integrate theoretical perspectives and conceptual tools from sociology with their study and practice of journalism. Successful students will gain a deep understanding of both disciplines, allowing them to pursue writing projects and cover current events through a sociological lens. The combined major has enough flexibility that students can study and write about the issues that most interest them.",
  "source_text": "Complete all courses listed below unless otherwise indicated. Also complete any corequisite labs, recitations, clinicals, or tools courses where specified and complete any additional courses needed beyond specific college and major requirements to satisfy graduation credit requirements.\nUniversitywide Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nUniversitywide Requirements\n.\nBA Language Requirements\nAll BA students are required to complete the BA degree language requirements, for a total of 12 semester hours of language study or demonstrated equivalent proficiency, as described in\nAdditional Requirements for BA students\n. Successful demonstration of proficiency does not reduce total minimum semester hours of study required to earn the BA degree.\nNUpath Requirements\nAll undergraduate students are required to complete the\nNUpath Requirements\n.\nJournalism Requirements\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nFoundation Courses\nC or better required in\nJRNL 1101\n,\nJRNL 1102\n, and\nJRNL 2201\n:\nJRNL 1101\nand\nJRNL 1102\nJournalism 1: Fundamentals of Reporting and Writing\nand Journalist’s Toolbox\n5\nJRNL 1150\nUnderstanding Today’s News\n4\nJRNL 2201\nJournalism 2: Intermediate Reporting\n4\nVisual Storytelling\nComplete one of the following:\n4\nJRNL 2301\nVisual Storytelling in Journalism\nJRNL 3370\nPodcast and Radio Journalism\nJRNL 5309\nNews Documentary Production\nJRNL 5310\nPhotojournalism\nJRNL 5314\nVideo News Reporting and Producing\nJRNL 5320\nPracticing Photojournalism: Community and the Camera\nLaw and Ethics\nJRNL 3550\nThe First Amendment and the Media\n4\nor\nJRNL 4650\nEthics and Diversity in the News Media\nJournalism Electives\nComplete four JRNL courses (two must be 3000-level or above).\n16\nSociology Requirements\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nCore Requirements\nSOCL 1101\nIntroduction to Sociology\n4\nSOCL 2320\nStatistical Analysis in Sociology\n4\nor\nINSH 3102\nIntroduction to Statistics in the Social Sciences\nSOCL 2321\nResearch Methods in Sociology\n4\nor\nINSH 3101\nResearch Methods in the Social Sciences\nSOCL 3300\nSocial Theory\n4\nSociology Elective A\nComplete two courses from the following range not used to satisfy other requirements:\nSOCL 1100 to SOCL 2999\n8\nSociology Elective B\nComplete two courses from the following range not used to satisfy other requirements:\nSOCL 3000 to SOCL 5999\n8\nCapstone Requirement\nSOCL 4600\nSenior Seminar\n4\nor\nANTH 4100\nMaking Anthropology and Sociology Public\nIntroductory\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nIntroductory\nSOCL 1000\nSociology at Northeastern\n1\nor\nJRNL 1000\nJournalism at Northeastern\nCo-op Preparatory Course\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nCo-op Preparatory Course\nEESH 2000\nProfessional Development for Co-op\n1\nor\nEEAM 2000\nProfessional Development for Co-op\nIntegrative Requirement\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nComplete one course from JRNL and one course from SOCL:\n8\nJRNL 3700\nData Storytelling\nor\nJRNL 5250\nGender in the Newsroom\nor\nJRNL 1949\nCovering Race in Pop Culture and the Media\nSOCL 3441\nSociology of Health and Illness\nSOCL 4520\nRace, Class, and Gender\nSOCL 4522\nEnvironmental Justice\nWriting Requirement\nCourse List\nCode\nTitle\nHours\nENGW 1111\nFirst-Year Writing\n4\nENGW 3308\nAdvanced Writing in the Social Sciences\n4\nor\nENGW 3315\nInterdisciplinary Advanced Writing in the Disciplines\nor\nJRNL 2301\nVisual Storytelling in Journalism\nJournalism and Sociology Major Credit Requirement\nComplete 81 semester hours in the major.\nProgram Requirement\n129 total semester hours required",
